  "title": "Lee2021 – SSVEP paradigm of the Mobile BCI dataset",
  "description": "This dataset contains the steady-state visual evoked potential (SSVEP) paradigm from the Mobile BCI dataset, recorded with scalp EEG while participants stood, walked, and ran on a treadmill. Participants viewed visual flicker stimuli at three frequencies (5.45, 8.57, and 12 Hz) across multiple sessions. It supports research on brain-computer interfaces that remain robust to motion and was reformatted to BIDS through MOABB.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a BrainAmp amplifier using Ag/AgCl electrodes (reference FCz, ground Fpz) plus EOG channels. Participants attended to visual flicker targets at 5.45, 8.57, and 12 Hz in 5 s trials while standing, walking, and running on a treadmill. Reported classifiers are rLDA and CCA.",
